    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass, including the new `Cp48` (fiscalYear) and `Cp14` (membership-number fiscal), plus the existing membership-points/level tests (`Cp39`, `Cp40`). Build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived owner values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, labelled `FY<YY>` from the year the fiscal period *starts* \u2014 so Aug 2026 \u2192 `FY26`).\n\n**New \u2014 `FiscalYear` helper** (`rest/function/owner/FiscalYear.java`): `startYear(date)` (July-or-later keeps the year, Jan\u2013June rolls back one), `label(date)` \u2192 `FY<YY>` (null-safe for legacy owners with no registration date), and `elapsed(from, to)`.\n\n**`fiscalYear` response field**: added to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (readOnly string, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains it), and wired in `OwnerMapper` via an expression mapping off the owner's already-business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`.\n\n**Membership identifier** (`AssignMembershipNumber`): the `-M<YY>` segment now uses the fiscal year's start-year rather than the calendar year, so it matches the returned `fiscalYear`.\n\n**Tenure** (`AssignMembershipLevel`): the +3 factor now triggers on **elapsed fiscal years** (`FiscalYear.elapsed(...) >= 1`) instead of a 365-day window. A new owner registers in the current fiscal year \u2192 0 elapsed \u2192 factor never applies at creation, preserving the level-4 cap.\n\nDescriptions in `openapi.yml` for `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` were updated to match the new behaviour.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: I read \"fiscal year starts on 1 July\" as *naming the year by its start* (1 Jul 2026\u201330 Jun 2027 = `FY26`), which keeps the existing `-M26` example valid. The tests only pin the `FY\\d{2}` format and internal consistency between `fiscalYear` and `membershipNumber`, not the naming convention itself \u2014 say the word if you'd prefer the end-year convention (`FY27`).",
